### 🔹 Line 2 — Environment Variable Flag

```ts
const ATTACH_SCREENSHOTS = process.env.ATTACH_SCREENSHOTS?.toLowerCase() === 'true';
```

**What it does:**  
Reads an environment variable `ATTACH_SCREENSHOTS`. If you set it to `"true"` before running tests, screenshots get attached. Otherwise, skipped.

```
ATTACH_SCREENSHOTS=true  → true  → screenshots ARE attached
ATTACH_SCREENSHOTS=false → false → screenshots are SKIPPED
not set at all           → false → screenshots are SKIPPED
```

**Why `?.toLowerCase()`?**  
Protects against `undefined` (if the env var is not set at all) — the `?.` means "only call `.toLowerCase()` if it's not undefined".

```ts
// Without ?.  → crash if undefined
process.env.ATTACH_SCREENSHOTS.toLowerCase() // 💥 TypeError

// With ?.     → safely returns undefined, which !== 'true' → false
process.env.ATTACH_SCREENSHOTS?.toLowerCase() // ✅ safe
```

