### 🔹 Line 4 — The `slugify()` Helper

```ts
function slugify(title: string): string {
    return title
        .toLowerCase()
        .replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, '-')
        .replace(/(^-|-$)/g, '');
}
```

**What it does:** Converts a human-readable step title into a safe filename string.

```
"Open the Cart!"   →   "open-the-cart"
"Login as Admin"   →   "login-as-admin"
"Step 1: Verify"   →   "step-1-verify"
```

**Why each line:**

```ts
.toLowerCase()              // "Open Cart" → "open cart"
.replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, '-') // replace spaces/special chars → "open-cart"
.replace(/(^-|-$)/g, '')    // remove leading/trailing dashes → "open-cart"
```

**Why do we need this?**  
The attachment name `step-0-open-the-cart` is used by `CustomReporter.ts` to match the screenshot to the correct step. Special characters in the name would break that matching.

