### 🔹 Line 8 — Get Current Test's Info & Counter

```ts
const info = test.info();
const index = stepCounters.get(info) ?? 0;
stepCounters.set(info, index + 1);
```

**Step by step:**

```ts
const info = test.info();
// Gets the TestInfo object for the CURRENTLY RUNNING test
// Each test has its own unique TestInfo
```

```ts
const index = stepCounters.get(info) ?? 0;
// Look up this test's current step count in the WeakMap
// ?? 0 → if no entry exists yet (first step), default to 0
//
// Test A: first step  → get(infoA) = undefined → 0
// Test A: second step → get(infoA) = 1         → 1
// Test A: third step  → get(infoA) = 2         → 2
```

```ts
stepCounters.set(info, index + 1);
// Save the incremented counter back for next step
//
// After step 0: set(infoA, 1)
// After step 1: set(infoA, 2)
// After step 2: set(infoA, 3)
```

