### 🔹 Line 9 — Take and Attach Screenshot

```ts
if (ATTACH_SCREENSHOTS) {
    const screenshot = await page.screenshot();

    await info.attach(`step-${index}-${slugify(title)}`, {
        body: screenshot,
        contentType: 'image/png',
    });
}
```

**`page.screenshot()`** — Captures the current browser state as a PNG buffer.

**`info.attach(name, { body, contentType })`** — Attaches the PNG to the test report.

**The name `step-${index}-${slugify(title)}`** is the contract:

```
step-0-open-the-cart
step-1-verify-item-count
step-2-proceed-to-checkout
  ↑        ↑
index   slugified title

CustomReporter.ts looks for "step-N-" prefix to pin screenshot to the right step
Allure v3 uses anything attached inside test.step() and shows it under that step
```

